When a line is drawn, it will normally “obscure” everything behind it as if you had used perfectly opaque
ink. It is also possible to ask TikZ to use an ink that is a little bit (or a big bit) transparent using the
draw opacity option. This is explained in Section 23 on transparency in more detail.

