26.3.2   The Colon Syntax II: Animating Myself
A frequent use of the animate key is for animating attributes of the current object myself. In these cases,
it is a bit length to write
[animate = { myself: = { :some attribute = {...} } } ]

in the options of a node or a scope. For this reason, TikZ allows you to use a special syntax with nodes and
scopes:
  1. In a hnode specificationi, which is everything following a node command up to the content of the node
     (which is surrounded by curly braces), you can write
          :some attribute = {hoptionsi}
     and this will have the same effect as if you had written
          [animate = { myself: = { :some attribute = {hoptionsi}}}]
