/tikz/on background layer=hoptionsi                                                                   (no default)
     This key can (only) be used with a {scope} or \scoped. It will cause everything inside the scope to be
     typeset on a background layer.
     The hoptionsi will be executed inside background scope. This is useful since other options passed to
     the {scope} environment will be executed before the actual background material starts and, thus, will
     have no effect on it.

