49       Circuit Libraries
Written and documented by Till Tantau, and Mark Wibrow. Inspired by the work of Massimo Redaelli.

49.1     Introduction
The circuit libraries can be used to draw different kinds of electrical or logical circuits. There is not a single
library for this, but a whole hierarchy of libraries that work in concert. The main design goal was to create
a balance between ease-of-use and ease-of-extending, while creating high-quality graphical representations
of circuits.

