56.4.2   Symbolic Rounding Operations
Commands in this section constitute the basic level implementations of the rounding routines. They work
symbolically, i.e. they operate on text, not on numbers and allow arbitrarily large numbers.

\pgfmathroundto{hxi}
    Rounds a fixed point number to prescribed precision and writes the result to \pgfmathresult.
    The desired precision can be configured with /pgf/number format/precision, see section 97. This
    section does also contain application examples.
    Any trailing zeros after the period are discarded. The algorithm is purely text based and allows to deal
    with precisions beyond TEX’s fixed point support.
    As a side effect, the global boolean \ifpgfmathfloatroundhasperiod will be set to true if and only if
    the resulting mantissa has a period. Furthermore, \ifpgfmathfloatroundmayneedrenormalize will be
    set to true if and only if the rounding result’s floating point representation would have a larger exponent
    than hxi.

