    further variables are defined. The first takes the name of hvariablei (e.g., \c) suffixed with x (i.e., \cx)
    and is assigned the x coordinate of \c. The second takes the name of hvariablei suffixed with y (i.e.,
    \cy) and is assigned the y coordinate of \c.
