58.5    Branching Statements
Sometimes you may wish to execute different statements depending on the value of an expression. In this
case the following keyword can be used:

if hconditioni then {hif-non-zero-statementsi};
    This keyword executes hif-non-zero-statementsi if the expression in hconditioni evaluates to any value
    other than zero.

if hconditioni then {hif-non-zero-statementsi} else {hif-zero-statementsi};
    This keyword executes hif-non-zero-statementsi if the expression in hconditioni evaluates to any value
    other than zero and the hif-zero-statementsi are executed if the expression in hconditioni evaluates to
    zero.

                             \usetikzlibrary {math}
                               \begin{tikzpicture}
