63.4    Shortcomings
Currently a number of things are not working, mostly due to the fact that PGF uses a 2D coordinate system
underwater, and perspective projection is a non-linear affine transformation which needs to be aware of all
three coordinates. These three coordinates are currently lost when processing a 3D coordinate. The issues
include, but possibly are not limited to:
  • Keys like shift, xshift, yshift are not working
  • Keys like rotate around x, rotate around y, and rotate around z are not working
  • Units are not working

  • Most keys from the 3d library are unsupported, e.g. all the canvas is .. plane keys.

