Shape star
   This shape is a star, which by default (minus any transformations) is drawn with the first point pointing
   upwards. This shape supports the rotation as described in Section 17.2.3, but the border of the star is
   always constructed using the incircle.
   A star should be thought of as having a set of “inner points” and “outer points”. The inner points of the
   border are based on the radius of the circle which tightly fits the node contents, and the outer points
   are based on the circumcircle, the circle that passes through every outer point. Any specified minimum
   size, width or height, is interpreted as the diameter of the circumcircle.

