80.4     Concept: Visualizers
Data points and axes specify what is visualized and where. A visualizer specifies how they are visualized.
One of the most common visualizers is a line visualizer which connects the positions of the data points in
the plane using a line. Another common visualizer is the scatter plot visualizer where small marks are drawn
at the positions of the data points. More advanced visualizers include, say, box plot visualizers or pie chart
visualizers.
