100.6    Error Messages and Warnings
Sometimes, a command inside pgf may fail. In this case, two commands are useful to communicate with
the author:

\pgferror{hmessagei}
    Stops the processing of the current document and prints out the hmessagei. In LATEX, this will be done
    using \PackageError, otherwise \errmessage is used directly.

\pgfwarning{hmessagei}
    Prints the hmessagei on the output, but does not interrupt the processing. In LATEX, this will be done
    using \PackageWarning, otherwise a write to stream 17 is used.

