    for each part of a single shape, two different shapes may very well use the same box even when the
    names of the parts are different. Suppose you have a circle split shape that has a lower part and
    you have a uml class shape that has a methods part. Then, in order to avoid exhausting TEX’s limited
    number of box registers, you can say

