108.2.3     Commands for Absolute Coordinate Transformations
The coordinate transformation commands introduced up to now are always applied in addition to any
previous transformations. In contrast, the commands presented in the following can be used to change the
transformation matrix “in absolute terms”. Note that this is, in general, dangerous and will often produce
unexpected effects. You should use these commands only if you really know what you are doing.

\pgftransformreset
    Resets the coordinate transformation matrix to the identity matrix. Thus, once this command i

