                               \pgftransformrotate{30}
                               \draw      (0,0) -- (2,1) -- (1,0);
                               \pgftransformreset
                               \draw[red] (0,0) -- (2,1) -- (1,0);
                             \end{tikzpicture}

\pgftransformresetnontranslations
    This command sets the a, b, c, and d part of the coordinate transformation matrix to a = 1, b = 0,
    c = 0, and d = 1. However, the current shifting of the matrix is not modified.
    The effect of this command is that any rotation/scaling/slanting is undone in the current TEX group,
    but the origin is not “moved back”.
    This command is mostly useful directly before a \pgftext command to ensure that the text is not
    scaled or rotated.

